    Copyright (c) Ryan Lauderback

The scripts/api/ auth and CRUD layer, doctor.sh and validate-spec.py
originate there, with local modifications: a new scripts/load-env.sh, a
separate state directory so this kit's refresh token does not collide with
the upstream skill's, trimmed CI, and validate-spec.py reduced to the checks
this kit can actually fire. Other inherited tooling (sigma-resolve.py,
workbook-manifest.py, harvest-workbook.sh, the Cowork/Cortex skill-packaging
harness, and 12 of validate-spec.py's checks) has since been removed as
unused here.

Plugin conventions -- the synthetic-fallback idea and POST /v2/plugins
registration -- were derived from:

    millersigma
    https://github.com/cmiller-coder/millersigma
    Copyright (c) Connor Miller

    whose plugin skills in turn credit neil-oliver/sigma-plugin-skills.

Two further conventions taken from there have since been dropped: the
single-file index.html pattern and loading the SDK from a CDN. Every plugin is
now a Vite + React project that bundles @sigmacomputing/plugin from npm, and
deploy-plugin.sh refuses anything without a package.json. The reason is in
docs/plugins.md -> "Why there is no hand-written-HTML archetype": a page that
pulls the UMD bundle from a CDN without loading React first leaves
window.SigmaPlugin a bare {}, and the plugin renders its fallback forever.

No code was copied from millersigma; plugins/_react-template/ is written from
scratch.

